Token formats

The token prefixes and shapes in src/rules.rs (for example AKIA, ghp_,
github_pat_, sk-ant-, npm_, pypi-) are taken from the public documentation
of the vendors that issue them.

If a detection rule is adapted from gitleaks or betterleaks (both MIT
licensed), their copyright notice is reproduced below, as their licenses
require. Rules are never taken from AGPL or CC-BY-SA sources.

(No third-party notices yet.)

Test fixtures

Every credential under tests/fixtures is fake: the AWS key is the example
access key from the AWS documentation, and the rest are real token prefixes
followed by the filler "FAKE". None of them work anywhere.
